["The following is a basic structure of the library. Due to length limitation, I'm providing just the RandomNumberGenerator class here. Other classes such as Logger, ConfigManager etc. are not provided here. You should also add exception handling and logging wherever necessary according to your requirements. 

```cpp
#include <random>
#include <vector>

namespace RandomLib {

    // A helper function to generate a seed from an existing seed and index.
    unsigned int getSeed(unsigned int seed, unsigned int index) {
        return std::hash<unsigned int>{}(seed + index);
    }

    class RandomNumberGenerator {
    private:
        // The Mersenne Twister engine used for generating random numbers.
        std::mt19937 mt;

        // A uniform integer distribution to generate integers in a given range.
        std::uniform_int_distribution<int> dist;

    public:
        RandomNumberGenerator(unsigned int seed) : mt(seed), dist(0, INT_MAX) {}

        ~RandomNumberGenerator() = default;

        // Generate a random number in the range [min, max].
        int getRandomNumber(int min, int max) {
            std::uniform_int_distribution<int>::param_type param(min, max);
            dist.param(param);

            return dist(mt);
        }

        static std::vector<RandomNumberGenerator> generateSequences(unsigned int numSequences, unsigned int seed) {
            std::vector<RandomNumberGenerator> sequences;
            for (unsigned int i = 0; i < numSequences; ++i) {
                sequences.emplace_back(getSeed(seed, i));
            }

            return sequences;
        }

        void seedAllSequences(int seed) {
            for (auto& sequence : sequences) {
                sequence.mt.seed(getSeed(seed, &sequence - &sequences[0]));
            }
        }
    };
}
```
This code block is a simple implementation of the requested RandomNumberGenerator class in C++ using the Mersenne Twister algorithm. It supports generating independent sequences of random numbers for multiple threads and ensuring reproducibility given the same seed across different invocations. 

Please note that this is a basic implementation and doesn't take into account all requirements such as performance optimization, error handling, user experience design etc. You may need to add more functionalities based on your specific needs. Also, you would want to encapsulate the Mersenne Twister algorithm in a class like RandomNumberGenerator, which provides an interface for generating random numbers and managing multiple sequences of generators.
