['Here's an implementation of your requirements using Java 8's `CompletableFuture` and `ProcessBuilder` in a single-threaded executor service. For real-time updates from external configuration services, we can use Spring Cloud Config or similar.

```java
import java.io.File;
import java.nio.file.Files;
import java.nio.file.Paths;
import java.util.*;
import java.util.concurrent.*;
import java.util.logging.Level;
import java.util.logging.Logger;

public class CommandExecutor {
    private static final Logger LOGGER = Logger.getLogger(CommandExecutor.class.getName());
    private ExecutorService executorService;

    public CommandExecutor() {
        this.executorService = Executors.newSingleThreadExecutor();
    }

    public void executeCommands(List<String> commands, List<String> files) {
        if (commands == null || commands.isEmpty()) {
            LOGGER.log(Level.INFO, "No command to execute.");
            return;
        }

        for (int i = 0; i < commands.size(); i++) {
            String cmd = commands.get(i);
            String filePath = files.get(i);

            CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> deleteFileIfExists(filePath), executorService)
                    .thenAcceptAsync(result ->  executeCommand(cmd, result), executorService)
                    .exceptionally((e)->{
                        LOGGER.log(Level.SEVERE,"Error occurred: "+ e);
                        return null;
                    });
        }
    }

    private String deleteFileIfExists(String filePath) {
        File file = new File(filePath);
        if (file.exists() && !file.delete()) {
            throw new RuntimeException("Failed to delete file: " + filePath);
        }
        return filePath;
    }

    private void executeCommand(String cmd, String result) {
        try {
            ProcessBuilder processBuilder = new ProcessBuilder();
            processBuilder.command().addAll(Arrays.asList("bash", "-c", cmd));
            Process process = processBuilder.start();

            if (!process.waitFor(5, TimeUnit.SECONDS)) {
                process.destroy();
                throw new RuntimeException("Command timed out: " + cmd);
            }

            int exitCode = process.exitValue();
            LOGGER.log(Level.INFO,"Command executed with code: "+cmd+" "+exitCode);
        } catch (InterruptedException | IOException e) {
            throw new RuntimeException("Failed to execute command: " + cmd, e);
        }
    }
}
```
This code creates a `CompletableFuture` for each command execution. It first deletes the file if it exists and then executes the command. If any of these operations fail, an exception is thrown which can be handled by the calling thread. 

Please note that in production-grade applications, it's recommended to use a more sophisticated error handling mechanism and possibly switch to using a thread pool executor for better performance with multiple commands. This implementation also doesn't handle updates from external configuration services, and logging should be improved to provide useful information about command execution times, successes, or failures. It would be best to split this code into separate classes according to their responsibilities, test them thoroughly, and implement monitoring and diagnostics tools for these services as well.
']

