['Here is a basic implementation of your request using C# .NET Core, for simplicity I'm assuming that the external API supports chunked requests but does not support rate limits. 

Firstly, install necessary packages: `Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc` and `Polly` for resiliency and `Serilog` for logging. Install them via NuGet Package Manager.

```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc;
using Polly;
using Serilog;
using System;
using System.Linq;
using System.Security.Cryptography;
using System.Text;
using System.Threading.Tasks;

public class MD5ServiceController : ControllerBase
{
    private readonly IMD5ExternalAPI _api;
    private static ILogger _logger = Log.ForContext<MD5ServiceController>();

    public MD5ServiceController(IMD5ExternalAPI api) => _api = api;

    [HttpPost("reduceArrayMD5")]
    public async Task<IActionResult> ReduceArrayMD5([FromBody] int[] data, [FromQuery] int batchSize = 1024)
    {
        try
        {
            // Validate input
            if (data == null || !data.Any()) return BadRequest("No data provided.");

            _logger.Information($"Received request with length: {data.Length}");

            // Configure policies for resiliency 
            var retryPolicy = Policy
                .Handle<Exception>()
                .WaitAndRetryAsync(3, attempt => TimeSpan.FromSeconds(Math.Pow(2, attempt)));

            var result = await retryPolicy.ExecuteAsync(async () => 
            {
                // Process data in batches
                for (var i = 0; i < data.Length; i += batchSize)
                {
                    var chunk = new ArraySegment<int>(data, i, Math.Min(batchSize, data.Length - i));

                    // Calculate MD5 hash of the chunk in parallel with other chunks 
                    await Task.WhenAll(chunk.Select(_api.ComputeMD5Async));
                }
            });

            _logger.Information("Request processed successfully.");

            return Ok();
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            _logger.Error(ex, "An error occurred during processing the request");
            return StatusCode(500);
        }
    }
}
```
This is just a basic example to demonstrate how you can implement your requirements. It uses Polly for resiliency and Serilog for logging. For the external API, an interface `IMD5ExternalAPI` with async method `ComputeMD5Async(int)` needs to be implemented. In production code, more comprehensive error handling should also be done. 

It's also important to consider how this service will scale and handle high loads as you would need to manage rate limits imposed by the external API and make sure your system is horizontally scalable when needed. You may use techniques like load balancing, sharding etc. depending on your needs. 

It's also a good idea to implement some tests for `ReduceArrayMD5` method using appropriate testing framework like xUnit or NUnit. Tests should verify correctness of the reduction logic and behavior under various conditions. 

Please adjust this example according to your exact requirements, as they can be quite different based on specifics of the external API you are using and how resiliency, performance etc. is handled in production environment.
']

