        handleErrors();

    EVP_MD_CTX_free(mdctx);
}
```
This code creates a simple SHA-256 hash from an input string. The OpenSSL library is used for the cryptographic operation. Note that error handling has been simplified in this example. In a real-world application, you would want to provide more robust error handling mechanisms. 

Creating a block cipher using OpenSSL:
```c
void encrypt(unsigned char *plaintext, int plaintext_len, unsigned char *key,
            unsigned char *iv, unsigned char *ciphertext) {
    EVP_CIPHER_CTX *ctx;

    if(!(ctx = EVP_CIPHER_CTX_new())) 
        handleErrors();

    if(1 != EVP_EncryptInit_ex(ctx, EVP_aes_256_cbc(), NULL, key, iv))
        handleErrors();

    int len;

    if(1 != EVP_EncryptUpdate(ctx, ciphertext, &len, plaintext, plaintext_len))
        handleErrors();

    ciphertext_len = len;

    if(1 != EVP_EncryptFinal_ex(ctx, ciphertext + len, &len)) 
        handleErrors();

    ciphertext_len += len;

    EVP_CIPHER_CTX_free(ctx);
}
```
This code encrypts a plain text using AES-256 in CBC mode. 

