To ensure fault tolerance and robustness against hardware failures, you might want to design the system in such a way that it can be easily restarted after such an event, saving current session states to disk or database, and recovering them upon startup. You could also consider replicating your data across multiple servers for better reliability.

As far as scalability is concerned, ensuring efficient use of memory, minimizing latency and maximizing throughput will depend on many factors including the specific requirements of your application and hardware environment. 

Unit tests and integration tests would ideally involve creating a test suite with functions to verify that sessions can be added correctly, updated correctly, retrieved correctly, etc., using various inputs. These tests should also check that error handling works as expected and that rollover averages are calculated correctly over time windows.
