3. **API Usage Monitoring** - Keep track of API usage by counting requests or implementing a rate limiter:
```php
class RateLimiter
{
    private $requests = [];
    private $limit;
    public function __construct($limit) {
        $this->limit = $limit;
    }
    public function checkRequest() {
        // remove old requests older than 1 minute
        $now = time();
        while (count($this->requests) > 0 && $this->requests[0] < $now - 60) {
            array_shift($this->requests);
        }
        if (count($this->requests) >= $this->limit) {
            throw new Exception('Rate limit exceeded');
        }
        $this->requests[] = $now;
    }
}
```
4. **System Health Metrics** - You can use tools like New Relic or DataDog to monitor and track system health metrics. 

