['Here's an example of how you might approach this task in JavaScript within an AngularJS application. This code block sets up your test framework, provides basic error handling, and logs details to the console.

```javascript
angular.module('app', [])
  .controller('TestController', ['$scope', '$q', function ($scope, $q) {
    $scope.testModule = function(testLabel, testCaseFunction, fieldNames, externalServiceEndpoints) {
      var promises = [];

      // Iterate over each external service endpoint
      externalServiceEndpoints.forEach(function(url) {
        // Perform the AJAX request asynchronously with Promises
        var promise = $http({method: 'GET', url: url});

        // Add the Promise to our list of promises
        promises.push(promise);
      });

      // Wait for all the Promises to resolve, or at least one to reject
      $q.allSettled(promises)
        .then(function() {
          console.log('All services loaded successfully');

          // Perform each test case and handle errors
          var result;
          try {
            result = testCaseFunction();

            // Refresh specific dialog fields if successful
            fieldNames.forEach(function(fieldName) {
              if ($scope[fieldName]) {
                $scope[fieldName] = '';  // Clear the field value

                // Send a message to the parent window with the field name
                window.parent.postMessage({ field: fieldName }, '*');
              } else {
                console.warn(`Field "${fieldName}" not found in module scope`);
              }
            });
          } catch (error) {
            // Log and handle the error, preventing it from halting test execution
            console.error(`Test case "${testLabel}" failed: ${error}`);

            return;  // Don't continue processing if there was an error
          }

          // Reset mocking library 'blueslip' to ensure accurate results for subsequent tests
          blueslip.reset();
        });
    };
  }]);
```

This code uses the `$http` service to make asynchronous requests to each external service endpoint, and stores these promises in an array using `forEach()`. It then waits for all of these promises to resolve with `$q.allSettled(promises)` before proceeding to run the test case function. 

The test case function is run inside a try/catch block to catch any errors that occur during its execution and avoid interrupting the rest of the tests. If an error occurs, it's logged to the console, but doesn't prevent subsequent tests from running. Finally, after each test case runs, `blueslip` is reset for the next test run. 

The function asynchronously loads and executes external service calls without blocking the UI thread, making use of JavaScript's event-driven programming model to manage this asynchronous behavior. It also logs detailed information to the console during each execution step. This allows for a clear view of any errors that may occur while running tests.
']

