For implementing auto-scaling in Kubernetes, we can use the Kubernetes Java API:

```java
public class AutoScaler {

    public void scaleUp(String deploymentName) throws IOException {
        try (KubernetesClient client = new DefaultKubernetesClient()) {
            // Increase replicas of the specified deployment
            Scale scale = client.apps().deployments().inNamespace("default").withName(deploymentName).get().getStatus().getReplicas();
            int currentReplicas = scale.getReplicas();

            if (currentReplicas > 0) {
                // Double the number of replicas
                Scale updatedScale = new ScaleBuilder()
                        .withApiVersion(scale.getAPIVersion())
                        .withKind(scale.getKind())
                        .editOrNewMetadata().build();

                client.apps().deployments().inNamespace("default").withName(deploymentName).updateScale(deploymentName, updatedScale);
            } else {
                System.out.println("No replicas available to scale up.");
            }
        }
    }
}
```

