Please note that the actual implementation will require significant more code than what has been presented here due to complexity of this task, and it's beyond the scope of this platform to provide such an extensive code solution. This code block will serve as a starting point or guidance for implementing the required functionality:

```rust
extern crate tokio;
#[macro_use]
extern crate lazy_static;
extern crate anyhow;
extern crate backoff;
extern crate log;

use std::sync::Arc;
use std::fs::File;
use std::io::{self, Read};
use tokio::task::JoinHandle;
use backoff::Backoff;
use anyhow::Result;

lazy_static::lazy_static![
    LOG: log::Log = log::new(log::Settings::default().level(log::LevelFilter::Info))
];

mod parser;
mod validator;
mod llvmir_generator;
use parser::Parser;
use validator::Validator;
use llvmir_generator::LLVMIRGenerator;

pub struct Converter {
    parser: Arc<dyn Parser + Send + Sync>,
    validator: Arc<dyn Validator + Send + Sync>,
    llvmir_gen: Arc<dyn LLVMIRGenerator + Send + Sync>,
}

impl Converter {
    fn new(parser: Parser, validator: Validator, llvmir_gen: LLVMIRGenerator) -> Self {
        Converter{ parser: Arc::new(parser), validator: Arc::new(validator), llvmir_gen: Arc::new(llvmir_gen)}
    }

    fn convert(&self, path: &str) -> Result<()> {
        let mut file = File::open(path)?;
        let mut contents = String::new();
        file.read_to_string(&mut contents)?;

        // Validate grammar using third party service
        let backoff = Backoff::default();
        loop {
            match self.validator.validate(&contents) {
                Ok(_) => break, 
                Err(e) => {
                    log::error(&format_args_err(e));
                    tokio::time::delay_for(backoff.next_interval()).await;
                }
            }
        }

        // Parse grammar and generate ASTs
        let asts = self.parser.parse(&contents)?;

        // Convert ASTs to LLVM IR
        for ast in asts {
            self.llvmir_gen.generate(ast);
        }

        Ok(())
    }

    pub async fn convert_async(&self, path: &str) -> JoinHandle<Result<()>> {
        tokio::spawn(async move {
            self.convert(path).await;
        })
    }
}
```
This is a simplified code block and does not cover all the required functionality such as creating appropriate structures for grammar, parser and validator modules etc. Also, it's assumed that all errors will be logged and handled within this module. It also assumes that external dependencies are implemented correctly elsewhere. 

You should also consider how you want to handle failures and edge cases in your actual implementation. This code does not include error handling for invalid or malformed input or other potential issues, but it provides a basic structure for implementing such functionality in a production environment.
