Then, a framework class:

```java
import java.util.*;
import java.util.concurrent.*;

public class TaskOrchestratorFramework {

    private final ExecutorService executor;
    private final LinkedBlockingQueue<AbstractTask> tasksQueue;

    public TaskOrchestratorFramework(int numThreads) {
        this.executor = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(numThreads);
        this.tasksQueue = new LinkedBlockingQueue<>();

        for (int i = 0; i < numThreads; ++i) {
            executor.execute(() -> {
                try {
                    while (!Thread.currentThread().isInterrupted()) {
                        AbstractTask task = tasksQueue.take();
                        task.run();
                    }
                } catch (InterruptedException e) {
                    Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
                }
            });
        }
    }

    public void submitTask(AbstractTask task) {
        tasksQueue.add(task);
    }
}
```

And then, a specific task:

