      LogEntry entry;
      fread(&entry, sizeof(LogEntry), 1, logfile);

      pthread_t thread;
      if (pthread_create(&thread, NULL, processLog, &entry) != 0) {
         printf("Failed to create a new thread\n");
         return 1;
      }
   }

   // Aggregate and send reports in real-time

   fclose(logfile);
   return 0;
}
```
This is just a basic starting point and doesn't cover all the requirements. It also assumes that log entries are fixed size, which might not be the case in reality. You would need to define your own struct for `LogEntry` or use some existing library/framework to handle logs if you plan on implementing this.
